Rules/Check/Damage: Check the text: "$text$" in <<damage>> is no known damage word
Rules/Check/DamageType: Check the text: <<damage "$text$">> names no damage type
Rules/Check/Kind: Check the text: <<unit>> knows no kind "$kind$"
Rules/Check/NoRules: Check the text: <<$type$>> needs a ruleset that knows it
Rules/Check/NoUnit: Check the text: <<unit $text$>> needs a unit or a kind
Rules/Check/Term: Check the text: <<term>> knows no "$id$"
Rules/Check/Unit: Check the text: no known unit in <<unit "$text$">>
Rules/Check/Variant: Check the text: <<term $id$>> has no variant "$variant$"
Rules/Mode/all: one language for all:
Rules/Mode/domain: per domain (in the table)
Rules/Mode/wiki: the wiki language
Secret/DMOnly: Secret: DM only
Secret/For: Secret: $names$
Section/Check/Inside: Check the text: a short form <<$macro$>> inside another block does not count - use the block form there
Section/Check/Nested: Check the text: $kind$ nested in each other - the inner one does not count
Section/Check/NoCharacter: Check the text: a lock names "$name$", who is no player character
Section/Check/SecretMidText: Check the text: <<secret>> in the middle of a section has no effect - put it at the start of the section, or use <$secret>…</$secret>
Section/Check/WrongType: Check the text: <<$macro$>> counts only in a tiddler tagged $type$
Section/Kind/date: dated sections
Section/Kind/secret: locks
Section/Kind/spot: spots
Settings/Check/Version: $title$ needs tiddlyrpg-core $required$, this wiki has $core$
Settings/Check/VersionFormat: $title$: tiddlyrpg-core-version $required$ - write it as >=x.y.z
Settings/Hint: Settings of tiddlyrpg-core for this wiki. They are saved with the wiki and apply to everyone who reads it.
Settings/Problem/NoChoice: Several are installed and none is chosen - active is the first by title, $1$.
Settings/Problem/disabled: Set is $1$, which is disabled - active is $2$.
Settings/Problem/missing: Set is $1$, which is not installed - active is $2$.
Settings/Problem/type: Set is $1$, which is no plugin of this type - active is $2$.
